## Usage

Uses grouped Density. Default scale=width gives groups equal maximum width; area and count change normalization. Supports orientation, side, bandwidth, resolution, fill, and outline. Picking identifies the observation group.

Violin is a built-in template, built from transforms and simpler marks: import it from `hmplot/charts`.

<Note title="SVG and PDF export">

**Vector, except** in a 3D view that holds a mark with no vector form there (Points3D, Surface or another 3D mark, a Heatmap or Image, a lit or additive mark, a globe or polar frame): then SVG and PDF exports draw all of that view's marks as one image, and `mode="vector"` refuses it. In other 3D views the violins are vectors too, drawn back to front by depth (approximate where marks cross closely). A `fill` column stays vector. See [what is not exported as vector](/docs/export).

</Note>
